# Product Decisions and Support Contract

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M0 Decisions
Dependencies: None

## Purpose

Separate the user's approved intent from proposed implementation choices before writing the app.

## Tasks

- [x] Record plain-text notes, normal dragging, quiet shell UI, and audience-capture exclusion.
- [x] Explain that capture exclusion, shell omission, picker discovery, and process visibility differ.
- [x] Record the user's explicit Windows 11-first choice and separate Teams/Zoom/Meet/OBS qualification.
- [x] Write docs\PRODUCT.md with requirement IDs, proposals, non-goals, and proposed budgets.
- [x] Begin D02 under the user's implementation instruction: WPF/.NET10 and opaque-window spike.
- [ ] Choose exact Windows 11 edition/release/architecture and required product modes for G1/G4.
- [ ] Complete D03/D05 approval for no-tray recovery, hotkeys and Edit/Present interaction.
- [x] Owner handles permission/recipient checks outside the app; remove both acknowledgment gates permanently.
- [ ] Approve D04: local recovery opt-in, retention, plaintext disclosure, and explicit save behavior.
- [ ] Approve D06/D07: initial package architecture, text limits, and hardware-specific budgets.
- [ ] Resolve D08: owner-selected license, release destination, signing and maintenance ownership.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every implementation-affecting proposal is approved, rejected, or explicitly deferred with an owner.
- [ ] The finite required capture matrix is named; no requirement says all software is undetectable.
- [ ] Recovery and failure behavior are acceptable without taskbar/Alt-Tab access.
- [ ] No future feature is silently added to the v1 release gate.

## Completion evidence

- 2026-10-07 planning conversation: Windows 11 first; Teams, Zoom, Google Meet, OBS separately.
- docs\PRODUCT.md distinguishes approved requirements from D02-D08 proposals.
- October8: user requested implementation; experimental WPF preview uses explicit saves/no autosave,
  fixed no-tray recovery shortcuts and local-only speech. These are implemented defaults, not final UX approval.
- User chose Docker Desktop installation/start as their own separate action; do not install it automatically.
- Release/license choices, complete support matrix, resource budgets and final visual/accuracy acceptance remain open.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-08 03:04 IST - Owner explicitly requested no permission/rehearsal checkboxes or repeat confirmations.
- 2026-10-07 - Requirements captured and platform chosen; remaining decisions intentionally open.
